<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Fury Warrior DPS</h3>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="weapons-for-fury-warrior-dps">Weapons for Fury Warrior DPS</h4>For the first time in Cataclysm the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=46917/titans-grip">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_titansgrip.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Titan's Grip</span></a> build pulls ahead, a change which can be almost entirely attributed to the powerful <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78478/gurthalak-voice-of-the-deeps">
<img alt="Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps</span></a>. Due to the power of the proc on this weapon, and the high proc rate granted by Fury Warrior (most abilities that we press have a chance to proc the weapon in both main and offhand, and we can often see several tentacles spawned at once) Titan's grip pulls pretty substantially ahead of Single Minded Fury, to the point where using two LFR <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78487/gurthalak-voice-of-the-deeps">
<img alt="Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps</span></a> is better than the BiS weapon setup for <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=81099/single-minded-fury">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/warrior_talent_icon_singlemindedfury.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Single-Minded Fury</span></a> focused builds. While you can certainly still enjoy that playstyle, it is significantly worse than Gurthalak focused builds in this phase.<br/>
